//==
// # Curved witnesses meshed once per sweep (complexity sweep, chunk L5)
//
// The sphere, torus and cone laws of 07-validation/poles.laws.plato each meshed a fixed curved
// witness per law case through RoundZeroModelMesh, and the face-check laws meshed it again. A
// PoleWitness holds the model and its round-zero mesh, built once per sweep by the law runner, with
// the discretizations and face meshes the mesh was assembled from, so the whole-model laws and the
// face-check laws read one build. Not generatable: it holds a BrepModel and a ModelMesh, so the
// runner exhausts the Witness_* list.

// A curved witness model meshed once without refinement rounds or validation
// (RoundZeroModelMesh) under PolesOptionsAt(chordal, false).
// Invariant: Mesh is Model.AssembleModelMesh(FaceMeshes, Model.NumberMeshVertices(Discretizations,
// FaceMeshes)), FaceMeshes[f] is Model.MeshFace(f, Discretizations, Options.Face).Mesh, and
// Discretizations is Model.DiscretizeAll(Options.Face.Discretization, NoFloors).
// Whole is true when the whole-model claims (closed, oriented, Euler characteristic Euler, volume
// within the tube of VolumeModel's oracle, Gauss-Bonnet) are stated at this chordal bound; the
// face-check laws name the witness and face they state.
type PoleWitness
{
    Name: String;
    Model: BrepModel;
    Options: MeshingOptions;
    Whole: Boolean;
    Euler: Integer;
    VolumeModel: BrepModel;
    Discretizations: EdgeDiscretizations;
    FaceMeshes: Array<FaceMesh>;
    Mesh: ModelMesh;
}
